  'refuse-refusal': ['The noun refuse meaning waste beside the verb refuse meaning decline, with different stress and final sounds', 'Refuse meaning waste is a noun, commonly /ˈrefjuːs/. Refuse meaning decline is a verb, commonly /rɪˈfjuːz/. The stress and the final /s/ versus /z/ distinguish them.'],
  'grammatical-object': ['The window labelled as direct object in an active sentence and as subject in its passive version', 'In Sam broke the window, the window is the direct object. In The window was broken by Sam, it is the subject. Its semantic role as patient stays the same.'],
