  'substance-content': ['Twelve grams of sugar and eighty-eight grams of other ingredients making one hundred grams of cereal', 'Example: 12 g sugar per 100 g cereal is 12% sugar by mass. The remaining 88 g consists of other ingredients. Package size determines the total amount of sugar in a package.'],
  'polynomial-content': ['The polynomial six x squared plus nine x plus three factored into three times a primitive polynomial', 'Over the integers, gcd(6, 9, 3) = 3, so the content is 3. Dividing leaves 2x² + 3x + 1, whose coefficients have gcd 1. This uses the positive-gcd convention.'],
